## COMPLETE LEARNING PATH (12-16 Weeks)

### PHASE 1: FOUNDATIONS (Weeks 1-3)
✅ **Arrays, Strings, Linked Lists, Trees**
- Basic data structures and operations
- Fundamentals before patterns

### PHASE 2: LINEAR PATTERNS (Weeks 4-4.5)
✅ **Week 4:** Pointer Patterns (2-pointer, sliding windows, prefix sums, cycle detection)
✅ **Week 4.5:** Tier 1 Patterns (Hash, Monotonic Stack, Merge, Partition)

**Status:** Week 4 already completed; Week 4.5 in progress

### PHASE 3: TIER 2 + TIER 1 CONSOLIDATION (Weeks 5-5.5)
🟡 **Week 5:** Difference Array, In-Place Replacement
🟡 **Week 5.5:** Deque Operations, Advanced Sliding Windows

**Note:** Kadane already included in Week 4.5

### PHASE 4: NON-LINEAR STRUCTURES (Weeks 6-6)
🟢 **Graphs, Trees, Heaps**
- Deep dive into non-linear structures
- Use Tier 1 & 2 patterns heavily in problems

### PHASE 5: TIER 3 + ADVANCED ALGORITHMS (Weeks 6.5-12)
🟢 **Week 6.5:** Tier 3 Patterns (Fast & Slow extended, Reverse, Matrix, Encoding)
🟢 **Weeks 7-12:**
  - Graph Algorithms (BFS, DFS, Dijkstra, etc.)
  - Tree Algorithms (Traversals, LCA, etc.)
  - Dynamic Programming (DP patterns, optimization)
  - Greedy Algorithms
  - Backtracking
  - Advanced Interview Patterns

