## KEY PRINCIPLES

### 1. TIER-BASED LEARNING
- Don't skip Tier 1 (foundational)
- Don't learn Tier 2 before Tier 1 (not ready)
- Learn Tier 3 after non-linear structures (optional but recommended)

### 2. SPACED REPETITION
- Complete one pattern per day (90 min)
- Review same day (15 min)
- Practice 5-7 problems per pattern
- Sleep between days (memory consolidation)
- Light review after 2 days

### 3. INTERCONNECTION AWARENESS
- Hash maps used in Tier 2 patterns
- Monotonic stack extended in deque
- Partition concept used in in-place operations
- Tier 3 patterns extend basic pointer concepts

### 4. PRACTICE INTEGRATION
- Week 4.5: 20+ problems minimum
- Week 5-5.5: 15+ problems minimum
- Week 6.5: 10+ problems (Tier 3 extensions)
- Total: 45+ problems for pattern mastery

