## PATTERN INTERCONNECTIONS MAP

```
TIER 1: Foundation Layer (Week 4.5)
├─ Hash Map → Foundation for Tier 2, used everywhere
├─ Monotonic Stack → Extended to Deque in Tier 2
├─ Merge Operations → Used in algorithms Week 7+
└─ Partition → Used in quicksort, in-place operations

    ↓ (Linear data structures mastered)

TIER 2: Important Layer (Weeks 5-5.5)
├─ Difference Array → Range updates, extends prefix sums
├─ Kadane's Algorithm → DP foundation, extends arrays
├─ In-Place Replacement → Extends partition concept
└─ Deque → Advanced monotonic stack, sliding window

    ↓ (Non-linear structures: Graphs, Trees, Heaps)

TIER 3: Extension Layer (Week 6.5+)
├─ Fast & Slow Pointers → Linked list extensions
├─ Reverse & Two Pointers → String/array extensions
├─ Matrix Traversal → 2D array patterns
└─ Conversion & Encoding → String manipulation

    ↓ (Advanced algorithms: Graph, Tree, DP, Greedy, Backtracking)
```

